<newsitem itemid="218144" id="root" date="1996-11-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: World Bank sets 10 bln yen dual currency bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 10 bln yen dual currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Tokto-Mitsubishi International and Sanyo International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    *6.70	MATURITY    18.DEC.97</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL CURRENCY ISS PRICE  100.125   PAY DATE    19.DEC.96</p>
<p> LISTING    UNLISTED  PAY FREQ    ANNUALDENOMS (K) 500</p>
<p> NOTES     *COUPON PAYABLE IN YEN REDEMPTION IN NEW ZEALAND</p>
<p>		DOLLARS AT $NZ6,195.01 PER 500,000 YEN.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF WORLD BANK'S GLOBAL MULTICURRENCY NOTE</p>
<p>		PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
